     "FiveIsland_LostCave x15",
     "Lost Cave: named by somebody who took it (2.10)"
    ]
   ],
   "look": "THE STACK. The rock is dead hardware piled up: every face reads as thin courses of slab -- boards, drives, casings -- laid one on another, every other one a shade darker, a joint here and there; one course a block carries a strip of tarnished gold: an edge connector. A ridge's top is the top board, seamed once a block. Light: dull sage and solder-mask green; the floor is ash-brown grit with a chip of board lying in it (ROUTE 3 is ASHFALL); the bright floor patches become pale drifts.",
   "split": "SPLIT UMBRAL ASCENT (palette split now: a cold violet dusk, the same courses; its own tiles in batch G). THE WRONG WAY and the tunnel can keep the stack."
  },
  {
