   "look": "THE OUTAGE. Basalt that grew in the dark: the walls are tall columns, cut vertically (the stack runs across; this runs down), each column a lit left edge and a dark right one. Light: night indigo and blue-black, deep but never grey -- HALFTONE and the unread DOLDRUM own grey. VERBOSE (FLASH) shows it; unlit it is a 24-pixel circle in black.",
   "split": "SPLIT OTHER CAVE (palette split): the same columns in a palette that is not THE BLACKOUT's -- a pale mineral teal. A per-entry palette swap would make it never the same twice; that is a question."
